### HTML (index.html)
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Simple Website</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
    <button id="colorButton">Change Background Color</button>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### CSS (styles.css)
```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px;
}

h1 {
    color: #333;
}

button {
    padding: 10px 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
}
```

### JavaScript (script.js)
```javascript
document.getElementById('colorButton').addEventListener('click', function() {
    const colors = ['#FF5733', '#33FF57', '#3357FF', '#F333FF', '#33FFF3'];
    const randomColor = colors[Math.floor(Math.random() * colors.length)];
    document.body.style.backgroundColor = randomColor;
});
```

### Explanation
1. **HTML (index.html)**:
    - The `<!DOCTYPE html>` declaration defines the document type and version of HTML.
    - The `<head>` section contains meta tags, the title of the document, and a link to the CSS file.
    - The `<body>` section contains the content of the webpage, including a heading and a button.
    - The `<script>` tag includes the JavaScript file.

2. **CSS (styles.css)**:
    - Basic styling for the body, heading, and button to make the page look better.

3. **JavaScript (script.js)**:
    - Adds an event listener to the button that listens for a click event.
    - When the button is clicked, it selects a random color from an array of colors and changes the background color of the body to that color.

